---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About | ViridIQ — Strategic AI Consulting"
  description="Founded by a Cambridge MPhil nuclear engineer. Principal-led AI consultancy with awards, Innovate UK advisory experience, and production delivery across enterprise sectors."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h1>ViridIQ is a strategic AI consultancy that bridges the gap between boardroom ambition and production reality.</h1>
      <p>Founded in 2023, ViridIQ works with enterprise clients to design, build, and deploy AI systems that create measurable business value. Every engagement is principal-led — delivered by a founder who combines strategic thinking with hands-on engineering.</p>
      <p>We exist because too many organisations are stuck between two unsatisfying options: expensive strategy firms that produce slide decks but cannot ship code, and technical contractors who build models but cannot connect them to business outcomes. ViridIQ is both. The thinking and the doing. In one engagement.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Ali Safari</h2>
      <p class="founder-role">Founder & Principal Consultant</p>
      <p>Ali Safari is a Cambridge-trained AI engineer whose career spans nuclear physics, energy systems, and production AI — connected by a single thread: using mathematical rigour to solve problems that matter.</p>
      <p>He holds an MPhil in Nuclear Engineering from the University of Cambridge (Emmanuel College, First-Class Honours), where his research at the Culham Centre for Fusion Energy gave him the mathematical foundations that became his AI engineering career. His undergraduate degree in Mechanical Engineering from the University of Southampton (First-Class Honours) grounded him in systems thinking and engineering discipline.</p>
      <p>Before founding ViridIQ, Ali founded Farad.ai — a multi-award-winning B2B startup that pioneered AI-powered digital twin solutions for UK energy systems. Over several years, the team built production ML models achieving 85-90% forecasting accuracy, grew a cross-functional team of 15 scientists and engineers, and won three industry awards for innovation in AI-driven energy optimisation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Awards</h2>
      <article class="award">
        <h3>Most Innovative Startup of the Year — London & East of England | 2022</h3>
        <p>Recognised for breakthrough AI application in the UK energy sector — the regional innovation award covering London and the East of England.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="award">
        <h3>Small Business of the Year — BusinessGreen Leaders Awards | 2021</h3>
        <p>The BusinessGreen Leaders Awards are the UK's premier sustainability business awards, recognising companies making the most significant environmental and commercial impact.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="award">
        <h3>Start-up of the Year — Solar & Storage Awards | 2021</h3>
        <p>The Solar & Storage Awards are the leading industry awards for energy technology innovation in the UK, judged by senior industry figures.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Track record</h2>
      <p>Ali has delivered AI systems for clients ranging from a $730B global investment firm to Innovate UK's Strategic Innovation Fund — where he has guided the allocation of approximately £45m across transformative energy projects including AI, quantum computing, green hydrogen, and offshore wind.</p>
      <p>He currently serves as an advisory board member at the University of Southampton.</p>
      <h3>Advisory & institutional positions</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Innovate UK Strategic Innovation Fund (SIF)</strong> — Strategic capital allocation across Data & AI, Quantum Computing, Green Hydrogen, EVs, Interconnection, and Offshore Wind. Guided approximately £45m to date.</li>
        <li><strong>University of Southampton — Advisory Board</strong> — Contributing to AI and engineering research strategy.</li>
        <li><strong>Clean Growth Fund</strong> — ML consultant appointed by the £101m venture fund for biotechnology investment evaluation.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Why "Virid"?</h2>
      <p>The name ViridIQ combines <em>viridis</em> — the Latin word for green, living, and flourishing — with <em>IQ</em>, representing intelligence applied with precision.</p>
      <p>ViridIQ carries that principle forward: deep knowledge, expressed with precision, in service of transformation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Values</h2>
      <div class="grid two">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Rigour</h3>
          <p>Every recommendation is evidence-based. Every system is production-tested.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Transformation</h3>
          <p>We take what exists and create something measurably better.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Stewardship</h3>
          <p>We treat your data, infrastructure, and trust as assets to be protected.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Honesty</h3>
          <p>If AI is not the right answer, we will tell you.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Cta />
</Layout>
